  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed first floor rear element of the proposed extension by reason of its size, siting and flat roof design would represent an overly dominant, incongruous, and visually intrusive form of development, out of keeping and character with, and detrimental to, the appearance and character of the property and surrounding area.  This would be contrary to Core Strategy (2010) Policies CP30, Development Management Document (2014) Polices DMD11 and DMD37, London Plan (2021) Policy D4 and National Planning Policy Framework (2023).\r\r",
    "Insufficient information within the Flood Risk Assessment has been provided to enable assessment of whether the proposed development would result in an increase in flood risk on or off site and suitable flood control and mitigation measures have not been demonstrated, including the proximity to a culverted main river, this would be contrary to London Plan Policies SI 12 and SI 13, Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD59, DMD60, DMD61 and DMD62 of the Development Management Document (2014) and National Planning Policy Framework (2023).\r\r"
